From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 31/55] readconf: let MetricsPath turn metrics on only where it
 applies

The MetricsPath option set options->metrics to 1 before the check that the
block is active, and without looking at what Metrics had set. A MetricsPath in
a Host block that did not match turned metrics on for every connection, and
one after "Metrics no" overrode it, which breaks the rule that the first value
wins.

Turn metrics on only in an active block, and only if Metrics is still unset.
---
 readconf.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/readconf.c b/readconf.c
index 8488438aa..30604a849 100644
--- a/readconf.c
+++ b/readconf.c
@@ -1444,7 +1444,10 @@ parse_time:
 
 	case oMetricsPath:
 		charptr = &options->metrics_path;
-		options->metrics = 1;
+		/* a MetricsPath turns metrics on unless Metrics already said
+		 * otherwise, and only in a block that applies to this host */
+		if (*activep && options->metrics == -1)
+			options->metrics = 1;
 		goto parse_string;
 
 	case oFallback:
-- 
